{
  "title": "Wat heb je gezien en gedaan?",
  "goal": "Talk about familiar experiences with common irregular participles and three ge- spelling patterns.",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "content": "Wat heb je gezien en gedaan?",
      "props": {
        "level": 1
      },
      "id": "f131afe7-063c-4870-8445-82f8f2203be8"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "It is Wednesday 6 January 2027. Sofia and Noor continue their holiday catch-up at home. They talk about Christmas and familiar moments in Utrecht. In this lesson you will learn several common irregular past participles and three useful spelling patterns. Verbs are blue, subjects green, places purple, and new participles are bold.",
      "id": "7c88dfcb-26cf-4ff5-a38d-0940b96539f6"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "content": "Story: holiday memories",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "id": "4e9b7173-2e2e-43d2-994a-45643fca442b"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "props": {
        "turns": [
          {
            "speaker": "Noor",
            "text": "Heb je foto’s uit Valencia?"
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Sofia",
            "text": "Ja, ik heb foto’s gezien en veel gegeten."
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Noor",
            "text": "Wat heb je met je moeder gedaan?"
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Sofia",
            "text": "We hebben samen gekookt. Ik heb ook een boek gelezen."
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Noor",
            "text": "Heb je Nederlands gestudeerd?"
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Sofia",
            "text": "Ja, en ik heb een brief aan mijn moeder geschreven."
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Noor",
            "text": "Heb je veel gedronken?"
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Sofia",
            "text": "Water en thee. Ik heb geen wijn gedronken."
          }
        ]
      },
      "id": "73fab6e5-e342-4e36-9726-493822060a05"
    },
    {
      "type": "vocabulary",
      "props": {
        "data": {
          "words": [
            {
              "term": "de ervaring",
              "meaning": "experience",
              "forms": "de ervaringen",
              "example": "Dat is een fijne ervaring.",
              "id": "961f082c-458b-4217-906d-adf0f1099ec2"
            },
            {
              "term": "de smaak",
              "meaning": "taste, flavour",
              "forms": "de smaken",
              "example": "De paella heeft veel smaak.",
              "id": "2a746a94-1b33-461d-a6bb-90346b01f12a"
            },
            {
              "term": "de brief",
              "meaning": "letter",
              "forms": "de brieven",
              "example": "Sofia heeft een brief geschreven.",
              "id": "7c5d7538-5b0f-43de-9fc2-9723f8c2e202"
            },
            {
              "term": "zien",
              "meaning": "to see",
              "forms": "ziet · zag · gezien",
              "example": "Ik heb foto’s gezien.",
              "note": "The infinitive is familiar; this lesson introduces the irregular participle gezien.",
              "id": "78bef5e2-d32b-4bda-b201-0cc7086b1422"
            },
            {
              "term": "eten",
              "meaning": "to eat",
              "forms": "eet · at · gegeten",
              "example": "We hebben samen gegeten.",
              "note": "The infinitive is familiar; this lesson introduces the irregular participle gegeten.",
              "id": "ab4c858e-e688-4948-aadc-369be361b708"
            },
            {
              "term": "drinken",
              "meaning": "to drink",
              "forms": "drinkt · dronk · gedronken",
              "example": "Ik heb water gedronken.",
              "note": "The infinitive is familiar; this lesson introduces the irregular participle gedronken.",
              "id": "8735fcbb-0dec-4f08-9db7-98b79308c35f"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "ad6e5106-7af5-47e5-bf95-c8571026c780"
    },
    {
