    {
      "type": "heading",
      "content": "Three patterns with ge-",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "id": "f2593e2b-a18f-4e3f-943d-de1867fae221"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Review: many regular verbs use ge- + stem + -t/-d. Three common spelling patterns change where ge appears, or leave it out.",
      "id": "b879ca93-7fe7-4957-988a-7cb608f201e8"
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "content": "1. Inseparable prefixes be-, ver- and ont-: no ge- (bezoeken → bezocht; vertellen → verteld; ontdekken → ontdekt). 2. Verbs ending in -eren take one ge- before the stem (studeren → gestudeerd). 3. Separable verbs: ge goes between the prefix and verb (opbellen → opgebeld).",
      "props": {
        "variant": "grammar",
        "icon": "book-open"
      },
      "id": "2f4b00f1-847f-4869-bd08-2b1611d38c8d"
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "content": "In studied, the ending is -eerd: studeren → gestudeerd. Say the complete form aloud; do not add another ge- at the front.",
      "props": {
        "variant": "pronunciation",
        "icon": "volume-2"
      },
      "id": "a464afe4-6af5-478c-b00f-da4312dfcf03"
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "content": "A prefix stays attached in an inseparable verb: bezoeken. A separable prefix moves in a present main clause, but stays around ge in the participle: opbellen → opgebeld.",
      "props": {
        "variant": "hint",
        "icon": "lightbulb"
      },
      "id": "2b6ab13a-96f0-4321-aa86-8fd19ab86732"
    },
    {
      "type": "numberedListItem",
      "content": "Check the infinitive: does it begin with be-, ver- or ont-?",
      "id": "f2c562a6-dbde-4811-b906-2a34771ed0af"
    },
    {
      "type": "numberedListItem",
      "content": "If yes, write the participle without ge-: bezocht, verteld, ontdekt.",
      "id": "bc2ca51f-be6d-463b-9c51-90ff60fe8ca7"
    },
    {
      "type": "numberedListItem",
      "content": "If it ends in -eren, use ge- before the stem ending: gestudeerd.",
      "id": "3f23f896-b6a5-4b65-b882-94a4dc5c4f13"
    },
    {
      "type": "numberedListItem",
      "content": "If it is separable, put ge between prefix and verb: opgebeld.",
      "id": "e11ad705-4e5b-484c-b6e5-4e16935e9903"
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "content": [
        "Sofia heeft haar moeder ",
        {
          "text": "bezocht",
          "styles": {
            "bold": true,
            "backgroundColor": "yellow"
          }
        },
        "."
      ],
      "props": {
        "translation": "Sofia visited her mother.",
        "note": "The inseparable prefix be- means no ge-."
      },
      "id": "e9075b1d-89ff-422a-9643-e5d8011f2e7a"
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "content": [
        "Noor heeft het verhaal ",
        {
          "text": "verteld",
          "styles": {
            "bold": true,
            "backgroundColor": "yellow"
          }
        },
        "."
      ],
      "props": {
        "translation": "Noor told the story.",
        "note": "The inseparable prefix ver- means no ge-."
      },
      "id": "fffbc697-d744-4715-b171-f83ba3ef632a"
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "content": [
        "Sofia heeft Nederlands ",
        {
          "text": "gestudeerd",
          "styles": {
            "bold": true,
            "backgroundColor": "yellow"
          }
        },
        "."
      ],
      "props": {
        "translation": "Sofia studied Dutch.",
        "note": "The verb ends in -eren: gestudeerd."
      },
      "id": "9e9f08a7-6964-4e39-8807-2e8b076dbafc"
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "content": [
        "Noor heeft Sofia ",
        {
          "text": "opgebeld",
          "styles": {
            "bold": true,
            "backgroundColor": "yellow"
          }
        },
        "."
      ],
      "props": {
        "translation": "Noor called Sofia.",
        "note": "With separable opbellen, ge comes between op and bellen."
      },
      "id": "eeb2c0f9-6fc8-4e29-b3e1-d26d79dcc047"
    },
